  "title": "Mixture of LLP and EM for a visual matrix speller (ERP) dataset from",
  "description": "EEG recordings from an online study with twelve healthy participants using a visual matrix P300 speller with a modified 6x6 grid extended by visual blanks. Three fully unsupervised decoding methods were compared: learning from label proportions (LLP), expectation-maximization (EM), and their mixture (MIX). The data support research on calibration-free brain-computer interfaces based on event-related potentials.",
  "methods_description": "Twelve healthy volunteers copy-spelled a 35-character German sentence in three blocks, each using a different unsupervised algorithm in pseudo-randomized order. Stimuli were presented with a 250 ms SOA and 100 ms stimulus duration, using two interleaved highlighting sequences. EEG was recorded with 31 Ag/AgCl channels (BrainAmp DC, EasyCap) at 1000 Hz, referenced to the nose.",
